      "The standard argument for gas is that electric machines cannot handle concrete, and the GPW3000 is the clearest counterexample in this guide. At 3000 PSI and 2.0 gallons per minute it produces 6,000 cleaning units, which puts it in the range of entry-level gas machines and roughly double what a typical budget electric unit manages. In our driveway testing it actually removed embedded algae and dirt rather than merely brightening the surface, which is where lower-output electric machines run out of capability. Build quality supports the output. The steel frame and larger wheels make it genuinely movable across a lawn or gravel drive, unlike the small plastic-framed electric units that have to be carried. The induction motor gives it the quiet operation and long service life that separate serious electric machines from disposable ones. For a homeowner who wants a driveway-capable washer but has no interest in owning a small engine, this is the most direct answer available. Two practical points. It draws substantial current, and sharing a circuit with other loads will trip breakers, so a dedicated 20-amp circuit or a heavy-gauge cord on its own circuit is worth arranging before the first use. And despite the pressure, 2.0 GPM is still below any gas machine, so a surface cleaner attachment is how you close the remaining speed gap on flat concrete.",
  },
  {
    id: "sun-joe-spx3000-electric",
    name: "Sun Joe SPX3000 2030 PSI",
    category: "2030 PSI, 1.76 GPM, Universal Motor, Dual Tanks",
    badge: "Best Budget",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 47200,
    pros: [
      "Very inexpensive while delivering usable 2030 PSI and a respectable 1.76 GPM",
      "Two onboard detergent tanks let you switch soaps with a dial rather than draining and refilling",
      "Total Stop System cuts the pump when you release the trigger, which extends pump life",
      "Light and compact enough to carry with one hand and store on a shelf",
      "Five quick-connect nozzles included covering every common task",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Universal motor is loud and has a considerably shorter service life than induction",
