    reviewCount: 8400,
    pros: [
      "Integrated hose reel is unusual at this price and genuinely useful",
      "Two-year full warranty, longer than most machines in this bracket",
      "Total Stop System protects the pump from bypass heating",
      "Onboard detergent tank plus five quick-connect nozzles",
      "Costs little more than the entry-level SPX3000 with meaningful upgrades",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Universal motor with the same longevity limitations as budget machines",
      "Water volume of 1.65 GPM is modest, so concrete work is slow",
      "Plastic construction throughout",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "A worthwhile step up from the entry-level model, mostly for the hose reel and warranty. Same motor limitations apply.",
    description:
      "The SPX4001 sits a step above Sun Joe entry-level machine, and the upgrades are practical rather than headline specifications. The most useful is an integrated hose reel, which is rare at this price and solves a genuinely annoying problem: high-pressure hose is stiff, holds kinks, and turns into a tangle on the garage floor, and a reel keeps it manageable and prevents the crushing and kinking that eventually causes a hose to burst. It also carries a longer full warranty than most machines in this price bracket, which is worth something given that the category has a reputation for short lives. The Total Stop System is present, cutting the pump when the trigger releases, and an onboard detergent tank plus five quick-connect nozzles cover normal tasks. At 2030 PSI and 1.65 gallons per minute it produces around 3,350 cleaning units, enough for siding, decks, fences, and vehicles. The core limitation is unchanged from the cheaper model: it uses a universal motor, which means it is louder, runs hotter, fades during long sessions, and has a service life measured in seasons rather than a decade. If longevity is your priority, the Westinghouse or Ryobi induction machines are the better purchases. If you want the entry-level machine with a hose reel and a better warranty, this delivers exactly that.",
  },
];

const schema = {
