        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The single biggest difference between an electric pressure washer that lasts a decade and one that dies in its second summer is a specification most listings bury or omit entirely: the motor type. Induction motors run cool, quiet, and for thousands of hours. Universal motors are loud, run hot, and are effectively disposable. Everything else about buying an electric pressure washer is secondary to getting that right.
